   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\) and \\( dv = x^{2} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = \\frac{1}{x} \\, dx \\) and \\( v = \\frac{x^{3}}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               3
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[\\frac{x^{3} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e} \\frac{x^{2}}{3} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( \\frac{e^{3}}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Exp",
               3
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{1}^{e} \\frac{x^{2}}{3} \\, dx = - \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{e^{3}}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Rational",
               -1,
               9
            ],
            [
               "Divide",
               [
                  "Exp",
                  3
               ],
               9
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( \\frac{e^{3}}{3} - \\left(- \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{e^{3}}{9}\\right) = \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{2 e^{3}}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
